    "text": "In Premasiri V. The Queen 77 N.L.R 86 it was held that:-\"In a charge of rape it is proper for a Jury to convict on the uncorroborated evidence of the complainant only when such evidence is of such a character as to convince the Jury that she is speaking the truth.\"",
